  "deactivated_at": "2026-08-30T16:13:36.686590+00:00",
  "detailed_description": "The Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana: Ice Plant/Cold Storage of Minimum 50-Ton Capacity , introduced by the Ministry Of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry &amp; Dairying, Government of India, aims to provide financial assistance for setting up ice plants or cold storage units with a minimum capacity of 50 tons, supporting cold chain infrastructure under PMMSY. The aim is to reduce post-harvest losses and improve fish quality. This is a Centrally Sponsored Scheme, funded in the ratio of: 50% by the Central Government, and 50% by the State Government. The beneficiary must operate and maintain the plant and ensure supply of ice to fishers at affordable prices.\n<br>\n\n",
  "eligibility": "\n1. The applicant must be a resident of Haryana and possess a valid Parivar Pehchan Patra (PPP).\n1. The applicant must own land or hold a registered lease for a minimum period of 10 years.\n1. The applicant must submit an undertaking within the DPR/SCP, accepting full responsibility for operating and maintaining the unit.\n1. The applicant must provide ice at affordable prices to fishers.\n1. The applicant must submit a Detailed Project Report (DPR) or Self-Contained Proposal (SCP) in accordance with PMMSY guidelines.\n1. The applicant must hold a valid training certificate in ice plant or cold storage operation and maintenance.\n1. The applicant must ensure the land is free from legal issues and must provide a valid land title.\n\n",
  "exclusions": "<br>\n\n",
